(Title) Tj
T*
(Safety, tolerability, and lipid response after short-term administration of TLC-2716 in) Tj
T*
(humans) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Selective targeting of hepatic lipid synthesis pathways offers a novel) Tj
T*
(strategy to address residual cardiometabolic risk. Methods: We conducted a randomized,) Tj
T*
(placebo-controlled phase 1 evaluation of TLC-2716 in adults with or at risk for) Tj
T*
(dyslipidemia. Participants received 14 days of once-daily dosing. Outcomes included) Tj
T*
(adverse event rates, laboratory abnormalities, and plasma lipoprotein concentrations.) Tj
T*
(Results: A total of 28 subjects completed the trial. No serious adverse events were) Tj
T*
(observed, and discontinuations due to tolerability were infrequent \(8%\). Triglyceride) Tj
T*
(levels fell by an average of 31% in the treatment arm relative to baseline, while placebo) Tj
T*
(showed minimal change. Postprandial remnant cholesterol declined by approximately 52% in) Tj
T*
(the active group. Hepatic enzyme activities and glucose homeostasis remained stable.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Short-term TLC-2716 exposure was well-tolerated with favorable lipid-modifying) Tj
T*
(effects, supporting progression to Phase 2 efficacy studies.) Tj
ET
